 "statement": "Annotated from the Beinecke scan alone (full page at 1900 pixels). A wheel with one clothed figure at the centre, in a short blue tunic, leggings, boots and a wide-brimmed hat, holding a crossbow low and pointing left, with a word in a different script at its feet. Around it are an inner and an outer ring of nude female figures standing with their feet toward the centre, without tubs, each holding a star on a line and each with a short label; four more such figures stand in a row on top of the wheel, outside the outer text ring, the leftmost one faint. The label groups in the transcription have 4, 16 and 10 lines; I matched them to the four figures on top (left to right), the outer ring and the inner ring. The four on top are a clear count; the rings are faint and crowded, and my own counts agree with sixteen and ten only to within one or two, so those two numbers lean on the label-group sizes. Ring labels were paired clockwise from twelve o'clock, an assumption about starting point and direction, so each ring's pairing may be rotated. Per-figure features are recorded individually for the four top figures (hair only, at low confidence) and are generic for the rings.",
